    "chunk_text": "Sir, our recent decision demonstrates how these different areas of Government policy could support our economic interests. On the 10th of July, 2026, Sri Lanka introduced Regulations, prohibiting the importation of goods mined, produced or manufactured wholly or partly through forced labour. Forced labour, first of all, is an issue of human dignity. Sri Lanka has long-standing international commitments against it: we ratified the ILO Convention No. 29 in 1950, Convention No. 105 in 2003 and the 2014 Protocol to Convention No. 29 in 2019. What has changed is the nature of international trade. Forced labour is now directly connected to market access, customs regulations, corporate responsibility and global\n\n\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dca\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bc8\u0bae\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) Hon. Deputy Minister, your time is up. \u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0db8\u0db1\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dcf\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b85\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bcd \u0baf\u0bb9\u0bae\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0bc6\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bbe) (The Hon. Arun Hemachandra) Sir, give me just one more minute.\n\nSo, these Regulations under the Imports and Exports (Control) Act that we have presented to this House are very valuable and important. We will make sure that, by making use of this opportunity, we would create more opportunities for us in the global trade environment and position Sri Lanka in a very important place within the global supply chain.\n\nThank you very much. \u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dca\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb